[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]Anatomy Rebuild[/color][/b] (optional, from the [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-anatomy/releases]GitHub releases page[/url])[/size]

Run [font=Courier New]AnatomyRebuild.exe[/font] after every BodySlide build and your outfits get the body's hip fix, so they stop parting from the skin at the groin in legs-up poses (a combat-armour leg on all fours: worst gap 5.10 → 2.25). It also removes the neck seam line. It never runs BodySlide and never moves a vertex, a morph or a slider, so any preset works, zaps included. [font=Courier New]--undo[/font] puts your builds back.

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-anatomy@276c3dc7df3ebbd7c28f53eeda1073ecfa0be936/docs/img/outfits.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109434]Anatomy Engine[/url] (fo4-ocbpc), then Anatomy.
[*]Get the [b]Anatomy Builder[/b]: the latest [font=Courier New]AnatomyBuilder[/font] zip from the [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-anatomy/releases]GitHub releases page[/url]. Extract it into a folder of its own (anywhere; [font=Courier New]Data\Tools[/font] works too) and run [font=Courier New]AnatomyBuilder.exe[/font] once. Vortex or no mod manager: double-click it. MO2: add it to MO2's executables and run it from MO2, like BodySlide.
[*]In BodySlide, pick "Anatomy Body" and your preset, then Build.
[*]Optional: the latest [font=Courier New]AnatomyRebuild[/font] zip, from the same page, after every BodySlide build. Keep its folder: the backups for [font=Courier New]--undo[/font] live beside it.
[/list]
Run the builder again after changing your CBBE or skin mod. [b]Built with an AnatomyBuilder older than 1.0.3?[/b] Run the latest once and rebuild "Anatomy Body": the older builders opened the entrance about 20% less than the tested body. It finds your game by itself; if it can't, run it with [font=Courier New]--data "<your Fallout 4>\Data"[/font].

[b]Why two downloads?[/b] Nexus quarantines any download that contains a program, so the Nexus file holds the game files only and the two tools live on GitHub, next to their source.

[quote]
[b]Needs:[/b] Fallout 4 1.10.163 (Steam or GOG, not next-gen), F4SE 0.6.23, the Anatomy Engine (fo4-ocbpc), CBBE with its BodySlide files, BodySlide, and a physics preset for OCBP/OCBPC, one that provides [font=Courier New]Data\F4SE\Plugins\ocbp.ini[/font] (tested with MadKita's Actual Jiggle). Anatomy's genital physics sit on top of it; without one it isn't supported. LooksMenu (nipples, glans colour), AAF (scenes) and MCM (settings) for the parts that use them.

[b]Body, skeleton and physics preset.[/b] Anatomy is built for CBBE's own 3BBB body (the "CBBE Body Physics" set in BodySlide); other bodies aren't supported. Any skeleton works, 3BBB included: the genital bones are added at run time. Your ocbp.ini and collision file keep working unchanged; only [font=Courier New]cbp.dll[/font] must be this engine's.

[b]Nothing of another mod is overwritten.[/b] Anatomy's physics lines sit in their own folder and are read after yours; the builder writes only new files, each in one step, and stops with a clear message rather than guess.
[/quote]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Is everything tested in game?[/b]
[spoiler]Most of it. Built and tested offline, but not yet seen in game: fisting and big-toy stretch, toys colliding as one tube, Rapport's MCM knobs for the physics, and the brows following vaginal and anal depth (the oral ones are confirmed). Known limits: in a two-hole position the aim chooses by geometry alone, men's own openings are not modelled, and the wrist can show a faint line against the hands. If you see any of this, please tell us.[/spoiler]

[b]What are the two tools?[/b]
[spoiler]The Anatomy Builder and Anatomy Rebuild are Python tools packed to run without installing Python. They are not in the Nexus download. Their source is in [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-anatomy]the public repository[/url] ([font=Courier New]tools/builder.py[/font], [font=Courier New]tools/rebuild.py[/font]).[/spoiler]

[b]Does it work with my other mods?[/b]
[spoiler]AAF and UAP, LooksMenu, Rapport, Silhouette (nipples stay flat under heavy armour it marks), Overture and Ivy (arousal sources), CBBE HeadRear Absolute Fix, any OCBPC physics config, and BodyTalk4 men.[/spoiler]

[b]Where are the settings?[/b]
[spoiler]MCM, page "Anatomy": the arousal nipples and their strength, rise and fade speed, each arousal source, and the glans colour. The sticky posts list every feature and setting.[/spoiler]

